'''Cholamandalam Investment and Finance Company Limited (CIFCL)''' is an Indian [[non-banking financial company]] and investment service provider, headquartered in [[Chennai]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Company Overview of Harvard Pilgrim Health Care, Inc. |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/research/stocks/private/snapshot.asp?privcapId=4493047 |access-date=5 March 2026 |website=Bloomberg |publisher=Bloomberg L.P.}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Chola to maintain 22-25% AUM growth in FY24 |url=https://www.thehindu.com/business/chola-to-maintain-22-25-aum-growth-in-fy24/article66838920.ece |access-date=1 June 2024 |work=The Hindu |date=11 May 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230523151502/https://www.thehindu.com/business/chola-to-maintain-22-25-aum-growth-in-fy24/article66838920.ece |archive-date=23 May 2023 |language=en-IN}}</ref> Established in 1978, it is a part of the [[Murugappa Group]].

As of 2024, the company has 1,387 branches across the country<ref name="fy24"/> and more than 54,000 employees, with the majority being in smaller towns.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/money-and-banking/cholamandalam-charts-out-future-growth-path/article28286418.ece|title=Cholamandalam charts out future growth path|last=Balachandar|first=G.|website=Business Line|date=4 July 2019 |language=en|access-date=2019-09-02}}</ref><ref name=BT1>{{Cite web|url=https://www.businesstoday.in/current/corporate/cholamandalam-investment-chola-group-profits-q4-results-quarter-4-march-quarter-fy-19-companies-results/story/341058.html|title=Cholamandalam Investment clocks net profit at Rs 291.86 crore in fourth quarter of 2018-19|website=www.businesstoday.in|date=27 April 2019 |access-date=2019-09-02}}</ref>

==History==
In 2005, [[DBS Bank]] acquired a 37.5% stake in Cholamandalam Investment and Finance Company, with the Murugappa Group lowering its stake to 37.5%. The company was subsequently renamed as Cholamandalam DBS Finance.<ref>{{cite news |title=DBS to pay Rs 228 cr for 37.5% in Chola Inv |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/finance/dbs-to-pay-rs-228-cr-for-37-5-in-chola-inv-105061701006_1.html |access-date=21 October 2024 |work=Business Standard |date=17 June 2005}}</ref> In 2010, DBS Bank sold its entire stake back to Murugappa Group and exited the joint venture.<ref>{{cite news |title=DBS Bank sells stake in Cholamandalam DBS Fin to Murugappa Group |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/dbs-bank-sells-stake-in-cholamandalam-dbs-fin-to-murugappa-group/articleshow/5779638.cms |access-date=21 October 2024 |work=The Economic Times |date=9 April 2010}}</ref>

